<title>MEXICO: Televisa says receives $650 mln in deal.</title>
<headline>Televisa says receives $650 mln in deal.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grupo Televisa SA de CV said on Friday that it had received about $650 million in cash and an equity interest of about 7.5 percent in the new publically traded PanAmSat Corp.</p>
<p>The transaction was tied to the previously announced merger between PanAmSat and the Galaxy Satellite Services busines of Hughes Electronics Corp.</p>
<p>Televisa also said it has received interests in Televisa's direct-to-home (DTH) Spanish-language broadcasting ventures in the Americas and Spanish previously owned by PanAmSat.</p>
<p>Televisa said it intends to use about $450 million of the net proceeds to repay indebtedness and the balance for general corporate purposes.</p>
<p>((--Mexico City newsroom +525 728 9559))</p>
</text>
